# Third-party notices

This file records provenance for third-party binaries and substantial third-party
code that ships with or is built alongside x86WASM.

## SeaBIOS (build-time / optional firmware binary)

- Project: SeaBIOS
- Purpose: Legacy x86 BIOS ROM for the classic PC boot path (Milestone 2+)
- Upstream: https://www.seabios.org/
- Source (QEMU mirror): https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/seabios.git
- Pinned revision: rel-1.16.3 (commit a6ed6b701f0a57db0569ab98b0661c12a6ec3ff8)
- License: LGPL-3.0-or-later (see firmware/seabios/LICENSE.notice and
  firmware/seabios/COPYING.SeaBIOS after build)
- Build script: firmware/build-scripts/build-seabios.sh
- Output location: firmware/seabios/bios.bin (gitignored; not vendored into
  MIT/Apache Rust crates)
- Manifest pin: firmware/manifests/seabios.json

No SeaBIOS sources are embedded in crates/. Building or loading the ROM does
not constitute a SeaBIOS POST integration claim.

## SeaVGABIOS (build-time / optional firmware binary)

- Project: SeaVGABIOS — the VGA BIOS option ROM built from the vgasrc/ tree of
  SeaBIOS; it is not a separate upstream repository
- Purpose: VGA BIOS option ROM for the classic PC video path (Milestone 2+)
- Upstream: https://www.seabios.org/SeaVGABIOS
- Source (QEMU mirror): https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/seabios.git
- Pinned revision: rel-1.16.3 (commit a6ed6b701f0a57db0569ab98b0661c12a6ec3ff8)
- License: LGPL-3.0-or-later. Upstream vgasrc/ headers state "This file may be
  distributed under the terms of the GNU LGPLv3 license" and carry both
  "Copyright (C) 2009-2013 Kevin O'Connor" and "Copyright (C) 2001-2008 the
  LGPL VGABios developers Team", so the ROM also descends from the older LGPL
  VGABios project. See firmware/seavgabios/LICENSE.notice and
  firmware/seavgabios/COPYING.SeaVGABIOS after build
- Build script: firmware/build-scripts/build-seavgabios.sh
- Build configuration: CONFIG_QEMU=y, CONFIG_VGA_STANDARD_VGA=y,
  CONFIG_VGA_VBE=n, CONFIG_VGA_PCI=n (plain 256 KB standard VGA; no SVGA
  extensions, no VBE, no PCI ROM header)
- Output location: firmware/seavgabios/vgabios.bin (gitignored; not vendored
  into MIT/Apache Rust crates)
- Manifest pin: firmware/manifests/seavgabios.json

No SeaVGABIOS sources are embedded in crates/. The emulator does not scan or
execute option ROMs; `emulator-cli --option-rom` maps an image for inspection
only.

Status as of 2026-08-09: the build script has never been executed in this tree
and no SeaVGABIOS binary exists here. The pin, the license notice, and the
build configuration above are recorded ahead of the first build so that the
provenance is settled before a binary appears.

